A||N||3||Red2m4||Vibration after Dogbone Replacement||||11||
Z||000000||Red2m4||04-30-2000||04:26 AM||||I just bought the dogbone rebuild kit from the fiero store.  Installed it, not too awful a job.  Now there is quite a bit of vibration and noise.  Any Ideas ?  My theories are.<P>  1. Poly bushing "sends" more vibration to frame.<BR>  2. While the engine was being rocked back and forth with out a dogbone I somehow messed up the exhuast system.<BR>  3. Now that the dogbone is tight, I'm detecting a problem with another motor mount.<P>  Any Ideas on how to fix? The car was whisper quiet before, now it sounds and feels like a truck.  Not undrivable, but annoying. <BR>  BTW - car is '86 2m4 , auto , 43k mi.<P>||||reg||11
Z||000001||batboy||04-30-2000||08:59 AM||||You're right, poly dogbone bushing will transmit more vibrations, especially with a 4 cylinder engine, but it should not be as bad as you're describing. If the dogbone went too long before getting replace, the lower mounts could of gone south too. It's worth checking.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ka4nkf||04-30-2000||02:40 PM||||The longer you use the poly dogbone the smoother it will get.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||04-30-2000||10:14 PM||||I have this in my 87. I'm betting you have an 86.5. Read on.....<P>look down at the tranny. Does it have a huge wrap around bracket with one tranny mount under the left side? Or does it have 2 smaller brakets with a mount in front and back of the tranny. The single mount is 86.5<P>Pontiac changed to the single mount for the 86.5 4 cyl w/ auto tranny. Polly dogbone bushings are a must with this setup. The dogbone takes ALL the torque load and the OEM bones don't hold up. (The dog bone only takes part of the load when the tranny has 2 mounts) An OE bushing bone in this setup can allow up to 2 inches of engine travel..... definatly not good.<P>The polly will transmit more vibration to the car. This can't be helped. It will wear in a little. On the other hand you don't have to worry about breaking the exhaust or beating hell out of the air cleaner TBI and intake against the trunk any more. (Check your trunk wall, I'll be very suprised if there is no contact mark from the air cleaner. I'll also be surprised it the exhause manifold isn't cracked.)<P>If the air cleaner has been whacking the trunk consider getting at least a new  mounting gasket for the TBI and make sure it's not leaking around the base.||||reg||1
